<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 86 0 R/E(The Pikes won the NCEFL Division 2 title in 1987\20588 and claimed their first major senior trophy in 1990\20591 by winning the North Riding County Cup. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

242 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 86 0 R/E(Promotion to the NCEFL Premier Division followed in 1991\20592, and the club narrowly missed out on the title the next season. Pickering also made its FA Cup debut in 1993\20594 and reached the FA Vase quarter-finals in 2005\20506.)/Pg 24 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

243 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 86 0 R/E(The club won the North Riding Senior Cup again in 2012\20513. After finishing as NCEFL Premier Division runners-up in 2015\20516 and 2016\20517, Pickering earned promotion to its highest level of senior non-league football. However, difficult seasons followed, including two curtailed campaigns during the COVID-19 pandemic and relegation from the Northern Premier League in 2021\20522.)/Pg 24 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

244 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 86 0 R/E(Since returning to the Northern League and then the NCEFL Premier Division, the club has faced several relegation battles, finishing second bottom in 2023\20524 but retaining its place. The following season brought improvement, with Pickering finishing 10th after briefly challenging for the play-offs. Off the pitch, Mill Lane has been significantly developed with floodlights, seated stands, covered areas and improved changing facilities. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

245 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 86 0 R/E(The club is also investing in its future through a scholarship programme, junior teams and the formation of a women\220s team competing in the North Riding Division 1 League.)/Pg 24 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

