333 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(RETFORD UNITED FC)/Pg 29 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

334 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(Retford United FC - A Brief History)/Pg 29 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

335 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(The club was founded in 1987 by Retfordian Brian Jackson to give the town a senior club after Retford Town had gone out of business. The club's inaugural season was in the Gainsborough & District League which was successful so it applied to join the Notts Football Alliance the following season and competed in that league up until 2001, when they joined the Central Midlands League.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

336 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(The incredible next several years of growth was attributed to local Retfordian Mr Dean Vivian. It was his financial support that built the ground, club house, floodlights, so much more, not to mention funding of the first team that catapulted Retford United's success. Just three years passed before another milestone was reached and the club joined the Northern Counties East League.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

337 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(The success continued, finishing as runners-up in the Northern Counties East League Division One in 2005\20506, gaining promotion to the Premier Division, which they won at their first attempt. They were then promoted to the Northern Premier League Division One South, which they won two years running, gaining promotion to the Premier Division in 2009. In all, between 2000 and 2009, they won a total of six championships, of various leagues and divisions, in nine seasons.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

338 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(However, at the end of the 2010\20511 season they finished bottom and were relegated to the Northern Premier League Division One South. Due to financial constraints, the club opted to resign from the Northern Premier League and to compete in the Northern Counties East League Premier Division where they again won the title in the 2011/12 season but they rejected promotion opting instead to continue in NCEL.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

339 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(Retford reached the fifth round \(last 16\) of the FA Vase in the 2006\20507 season, while their best run in the FA Cup consisted of one appearance in the fourth qualifying round, in the 2008\20509 season, where they were defeated 3\2051 by Alfreton Town. Their first season in the FA Trophy in 2007\20508 took them to the first round where they were defeated 5\2052 by Histon. Retford were relegated from the 1st division of the NCEL at the end of season 2017-2018.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

340 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 91 0 R/Pg 29 0 R/A[578 0 R 0]/K[7]>>
endobj

341 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 91 0 R/Pg 29 0 R/A[524 0 R 0]/K[8]>>
endobj

342 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 91 0 R/Pg 29 0 R/A[525 0 R 0]/K[9]>>
endobj

343 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 92 0 R/T(The club has been taken over by Nik Springthorpe. Bringing a lot of change to the club with a refurbished clubhouse, changing rooms and various outside areas of the ground. After two incomplete seasons due to Covid, the Badgers won the only silverware available as they won the Chairman\220s Cup in 2021 and then in the 2022 season they lifted the Notts Senior Trophy.)/E(The club has been taken over by Nik Springthorpe. Bringing a lot of change to the club with a refurbished clubhouse, changing rooms and various outside areas of the ground. After two incomplete seasons due to Covid, the Badgers won the only silverware available as they won the Chairman\220s Cup in 2021 and then in the 2022 season they lifted the Notts Senior Trophy.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

344 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(In June 2022, former player and Badgers legend Ryan Hindley took the reins and at his first attempt took the Badgers back up to the NCEL after winning the Central Midlands League by 17 points, only losing one league game! The Badgers reached the Play Off Semi-Final in their first season back in step 6 but fell to Beverley Town. We were moved sideways to the United Counties League for the 2024/25 season. Once again reaching the Playoffs but this time lost to Blackstones FC. Would things work out better for the Badgers come the next season\203)/Pg 30 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

345 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(The 2025/26 season marked one of the most memorable chapters in Retford United\220s history, as the Badgers finally secured their long-awaited return to Step 5 football. Ryan Hindley\220s side enjoyed an outstanding league campaign, accumulating an incredible 103 points. )/Pg 30 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

346 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(Despite that remarkable total, automatic promotion remained just out of reach, meaning the Badgers would have to earn their place through the play-offs. After overcoming Staveley Miners in the semi-final, they then beat Coalville Town in a dramatic final, with the game decided on penalties  )/Pg 30 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

347 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 92 0 R/T(On 14 May 2026, it was officially confirmed that Retford United would return to the Northern Counties East League, competing in the Premier Division during the 2026/27 season. On Friday 9th October 2026, following four highly successful seasons at the helm, Ryan Hindley tendered his resignation as manager after being presented with an opportunity to take charge of Step 3 side Ilkeston Town. It was an opportunity he felt he could not turn down, bringing an end to a memorable chapter in the club\220s history. His departure saw assistant manager Jas Colliver step up to take charge of the first team, marking the beginning of a new era at Cannon Park)/E(On 14 May 2026, it was officially confirmed that Retford United would return to the Northern Counties East League, competing in the Premier Division during the 2026/27 season. On Friday 9th October 2026, following four highly successful seasons at the helm, Ryan Hindley tendered his resignation as manager after being presented with an opportunity to take charge of Step 3 side Ilkeston Town. It was an opportunity he felt he could not turn down, bringing an end to a memorable chapter in the club\220s history. His departure saw assistant manager Jas Colliver step up to take charge of the first team, marking the beginning of a new era at Cannon Park)/Pg 30 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

